# Make a Node version mismatch fail the install instead of the test run.
#
# jsdom 30 needs Node >= 22.22.2 and reaches it through undici, whose webidl
# shim destructures `markAsUncloneable` from `node:worker_threads` - a symbol
# Node 20 does not have. On Node 20 that silently becomes `undefined` and the
# five jsdom suites die with "webidl.util.markAsUncloneable is not a function"
# on import, long after `npm ci` reported success.
#
# npm ignores `engines` by default, which is what let a workflow pinned to
# Node 20 install a tree it could not run. This turns that warning into the
# error it should always have been.
engine-strict=true
